profile: tinyrustlm.test-plan.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-09-27T17:15:02Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-working-product-memory-2026-09-19.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-09-19.md

gate_0_memory_and_intake:
  - Verify every manifest-owned report length/SHA-256, ledger entry, synthesis/TDD route, placeholder-only active intake, decision-index coverage, UAI size ceiling, no stale current policy, and no secrets.
  - Verify all ecosystem totem/taboo files state the two distinct MemoryEndpoints uses and synchronized prelaunch redundancy.

rust_engineering_review:
  review: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/rust-engineering-quality-review-2026-09-27.md
  local_baseline: After source admission, run local rustfmt, Clippy and affected unit/integration/doctests with locked dependencies and recorded compiler, target and supported feature combinations. Never enable hosted Actions.
  behavioral_tests: Pair round trips with independent known-answer and hostile rejection cases; cover arithmetic, allocation ceilings, malformed text, cancellation and transitions. Producer/consumer agreement can hide a shared bug.
  specialized_checks: Select bounded fuzzing for parsers, Miri for exercised unsafe invariants and Loom for custom synchronization when warranted and supported. Listed tools are not completed evidence; no dependency addition is implied.
  performance: Measure release workloads and native/browser phase memory, cold/warm latency and cancellation before optimization. Microbenchmarks cannot establish actual model or browser viability.
  limits: September27 intake validates custody/guidance only; source authority stops at unexpected E:\Source\Rust\.vs. No Rust execution, coverage, clean release or qualification is claimed.

gate_1_contracts:
  - Sole closed schemas, deterministic cross-language vectors, duplicate/unknown/trailing/overflow negatives, operation graph, exact member closure, and independent recomputation.
  - Keep former /10 parent/flushed forms negative; preserve /10 terminal failure.

gate_2_source_operation:
  - New remote-exact output-free registration; wholly new absent roots and identities; one launch; bounded streams/process tree/cancellation; restart safety; immutable terminal decision.
  - Exact pinned Qwen revision, file locks, license/provenance, streamed acquisition, contained conversion, and independent six-member inspection.

gate_3_composition:
  - Hostile-safe parsing, exact tensor registry/shapes, quantization semantics, tokenizer/model binding, Template2/Sampling2/Prompt2 closure, member digests, and no implicit defaults.

gate_4_numerical:
  - Check qwen3-numerical-execution-owner.test.js with NODE_V8_COVERAGE confined to owned canonical artifacts; Node otherwise auto-propagates coverage into explicit child environments. Assert canonical output rejection before capture creation, startup-variable exclusion, isolated pinned Python and exact owned cleanup. C29 records all 56 affected checks passing and the unchanged source scan still incomplete.
  - Bind fresh execution metadata and all imported helper dependencies before material launch; runner boundary fixes do not revive closed v2 registration. Keep model roots below D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM and require the unchanged source-authority scan to pass before writing output.
  - Current reference runtime is artifacts/external/qwen3-numerical-oracle/environment/Scripts/python.exe with contracts/vnext/qwen3-numerical-oracle-environment-lock.v2.json and qwen3-numerical-differential-profile.v2.json. The profile binds the prepared /3 owner and helpers; a fresh real v3 registration and complete material gates are still required.
  - C30 rejects all closed execution schemas, old lock paths, missing helper bindings, mismatched operation parents/dates, inherited skip allowances and promotion of rejected diagnostic ancestry. All 58 affected checks pass. Preserve exact numerical cases, thresholds and historical bytes; fixture validation is not real registration.
  - Before material execution, run the existing qwen3_numerical_environment_lock.py --verify-runtime preflight against the canonical lock using the intended interpreter; a training environment is not automatically the pinned numerical reference.
  - Run py -3 -B -m unittest tinyrustlm.tools.tests.qwen3_numerical_source_owner_test for typed environment failure propagation. See ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C27 for the focused Node checks and explicit unavailable-framework limit.
  - Pinned source framework to scalar-native first-divergence vectors at tokenizer, template, embeddings, layers, logits, sampling, and tokens.
  - Optimized native and real-browser WASM differential gates with preregistered bounds, resource measurements, cancellation, poisoning, and recovery.

gate_5_quality:
  - Untouched source screen, sealed paraphrases, multi-turn semantic invariants, raw outputs, fixed seeds, contamination controls, paired quantization/browser noninferiority, blinded human adjudication, and honest rejection.

gate_6_product_browser:
  - Restore eligible installed composition or automatically acquire the qualified MiniModel default through its admitted route; Advanced retains explicit local conversion. No instruction-file substitute or synthetic default.
  - Exactly-once rendering, real cancellation, worker replacement, responsive/accessibility/privacy assertions, process closure, owned profile deletion, and no unexpected network traffic.

gate_7_memory_endpoints:
  - Direct agent lane: scoped identities, authenticated meetings/messages/memory, conflict handling, handoff, and exact receipts.
  - TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lane: explicit user sign-in/consent, scoped token, write/reconnect/restore/conflict/replay/delete/cleanup, and exact receipts.
  - Cross-lane credential and authority isolation; synchronized secret-safe backup memory; no silent transcript promotion or upload.

gate_8_p2p_and_catalog:
  - Two independent process lanes per distinct qualified model, shared read-only store, hostile HTTP, exact pieces, outside signed proof, expiry/revocation, announcement lifecycle, and direct import.

gate_9_release:
  - Format, unit, integration, property, fuzz, package consumer, win-x64, linux-x64, physical linux-arm64 where claimed, WASM, Chromium, docs, accessibility, privacy, SBOM/provenance/signing/secret gates.
  - Clean committed pushed remote-exact source; synchronized docs/marketing/version/release date/log; authorized deployment; HTTPS readback; rollback.

current_required_checks:
  - UaixMemoryConsolidationTests and rewritten report-intake verification.
  - MemoryEndpoints portable policy and sync tests.
  - For this memory intake, run the affected memory/intake checks, pointer/hash/coverage-of-reports validation and diff/secret hygiene. Behavioral changes require their complete affected managed/Node/Rust/browser gates separately.

counters: Stay 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, 0/20 until exact live receipts pass the corresponding gate.

reviewed_diagnostic_matrix:
  reports: R01, R02, R03, R04, R08
  source_before_conversion: Exact source revision/weight/license admission, reference useful-answer screen, then converted runtime; unchanged rejected ancestry stays diagnostic-only.
  arms: original source; independently reconstructed quantized source; scalar Rust; optimized native where implemented; actual browser WASM.
  isolation: Original-vs-reconstructed measures compression; reconstructed-vs-scalar isolates conversion/arithmetic; later arms test backend effects. Teacher-force exact IDs before sampled free running.
  cases: one/two tokens; uneven lengths; repeated tokens; near-empty prompts; UTF-8/emoji/combining marks/whitespace/code/JSON; special-token data; multi-turn correction; edited/cancelled race; cache/context boundary.
  capture: IDs/serialization, embeddings, normalization, Q/K/V and Q/K normalization, RoPE/mask/attention, residual/MLP/final normalization/logits; bounded summaries then exact first-divergence slices.
  arithmetic: Per-operation absolute/relative bounds, low-value handling, NaN/Inf rejection, rank/top-margin changes; retain registered thresholds. Exact IDs/shapes/indices are not approximate.
  quantization: Hold model/template/sampler/input fixed across full precision, reconstructed Q8 and runtime. Test zero/outlier/tiny/nonfinite rows, rounding ties, byte counts, signedness and tensor orientation.
  browser: Measure real cold/warm phase peaks, TTFT/decode, main-thread responsiveness, cancel latency and multi-tab/reload/eviction behaviour; do not import report RAM/TPS limits as measured gates.

reviewed_quality_and_data:
  reports: R05, R06, R07
  invariants: Latest explicit correction wins; unresolved equal-authority conflict stays unresolved; missing resources/evidence are not invented; answers remain useful and source-grounded.
  scoring: Separate material failures, graded usefulness, format, latency/resources and feature-specific claims. Judge calibration/position reversal supplement deterministic parsers and real independent review.
  splits: Development, regression, selection and untouched holdout have separate roles; report examples are public development cases. Exposed holdout items need independent replacements.
  statistics: Report counts/denominators and representative-sampling assumptions. Zero failures in 280 independent representative cases gives about 1.064 percent one-sided 95 percent upper bound, not zero risk.
  pilot: Keep the frozen 1024 accepted-record allocation and positive-help ratio; obtain two genuine reviewers, independent adjudication and holdout custody. No invented preference labels or hidden teacher reasoning.
  training: Verify assistant-only masks, padding/packing, normalization, optimizer/schedule/precision and KL direction/temperature before bounded ablation. Require broad non-regression and post-conversion/browser checks before scale.
  proposals: New allocations/objectives/ranks, kappa/accuracy thresholds and performance budgets require explicit experiment decisions; never weaken a frozen gate.

reviewed_transfer_storage_release:
  reports: R09, R10, R11, R12, R13, R15, R16
  transfer: Seed-only availability, wrong/truncated/extra ranges, chunk identity, hostile peers, backpressure, cancellation and resumed hash verification.
  storage: Fault injection at every persistent transition; no mixed composition, unverified activation, stale-reader deletion, unexpected-file cleanup or indefinite retired model.
  release: First visit and existing tabs, cache/client graph consistency, interrupted publication, competing publishers and external readback; FTPS mocks are not remote transaction proof.
  end_to_end: Clean supported browser -> qualified default -> useful multi-turn answer -> offline return -> safe cancel/update; owner official acceptance remains distinct from all tests.
  memory: Verify all current pointers and every September report disposition/hash/proof route; preserve dated UAI and prior ledger body as history.
